LRC arc criteria for tournament-analysis loneliness metrics
====================================================================================================
Tie Hamiltonian path for every criterion: increasing runner label i -> j for i < j.
Strict arcs are reported separately from tie-path completion.

Criteria switchboard:
  phase_half                   vertices=all    observable=pair phase delta frac(x_j-x_i)
    switch=i -> j iff j is clockwise from i by less than 1/2
  lrc_close_sector             vertices=all    observable=pair phase delta frac(x_j-x_i)
    switch=strict arc only inside the LRC danger sector of width 1/n
  local_moat_min               vertices=all    observable=vertex score min(left_gap,right_gap)
    switch=larger two-sided local moat points to smaller local moat
  local_moat_sum               vertices=all    observable=vertex score left_gap+right_gap
    switch=larger adjacent gap sum points to smaller sum
  safe_deficit                 vertices=all    observable=vertex score local deficit below threshold on two adjacent gaps
    switch=smaller deficit points to larger deficit
  origin_distance              vertices=moving observable=moving runner distance from stationary runner 0
    switch=farther from 0 points to closer to 0
  origin_blocker_relief        vertices=moving observable=origin nearest distance after deleting one moving runner
    switch=runner whose deletion most improves origin moat points to the other
  origin_deficit_relief        vertices=moving observable=origin threshold-deficit relief after deleting one moving runner
    switch=runner whose deletion removes more origin deficit points to the other
  k1_relief_pressure           vertices=all    observable=pairwise nearest-neighbor deletion relief
    switch=blocker points to runner whose k=1 nearest moat it improves more
  k2_relief_pressure           vertices=all    observable=pairwise two-nearest-neighbor deletion relief
    switch=blocker points to runner whose k=2 nearest moat it improves more
  threshold_deficit_pressure   vertices=all    observable=pairwise relief of two-neighbor deficit below 1/n
    switch=blocker points to runner whose threshold deficit it removes more
  bracket_relief_pressure      vertices=all    observable=pairwise relief of circular two-sided local bracket
    switch=blocker points to runner whose adjacent safe bracket it improves more

